      "id": "bbc-2026-09-15-trump-says-kennedy-center-will-shutter-immediately-as-judge-",
      "title": "Trump says Kennedy Center will shutter 'immediately', as judge rules his name must stay off building",
      "summary": "The ruling came as the centre's Trump-appointed board was reportedly scheduled to vote on closing it for two years.",
      "body": "The Kennedy Center board has voted to close the performing arts centre for two years, just as a US judge blocked it from adding President Donald Trump's name back to the building.In May, the same judge ordered the removal of Trump's name and blocked its temporary closure for proposed renovationsThe board, which is chaired by Trump and comprises his cabinet members and allies, approved a resolution in August that called for the inscription \"Renovated and Restored by President Donald J. Trump\" to be added to the venue.Trump announced the addition of his name to the institution, among other rebranding measures across the nation's capital, last year.Trump wrote on Truth Social that the board voted \"almost unanimously\" to close the storied venue \"for safety reasons\" and to begin the process of reconstruction. While the closing \"will take place immediately\", Trump said renovations cannot begin until the court \"rules on the Board's approved name\" and vowed to take the case to the Supreme Court if it is a \"negative\" ruling.He added that the US Department of Justice will ask for an expedited appeal and that he had raised $17m for the centre to \"keep it afloat\". Also in August, the board approved a resolution to rename the campus the \"President Donald J. Trump Plaza\" if $100m was raised for the renovations.The judge's written order came less than an hour before the centre's board voted on the closure. This was the third time it has approved closing the centre since February, amid legal challenges to Trump's work to take greater control of the institution and memorial.In February 2025, he replaced several trustees on the centre's board and became the arts centre's chairman. Then, in December, the  board decided to rename the institution and new lettering bearing Trump's full name was affixed to the centre's front portico the following day.The changes, including the re-naming, were followed by cancellations by artists booked at the venue and a drop in ticket sales.Most of the legal challenges to Trump's changes focus on the fact that Congress established the centre as a memorial to President John F Kennedy, who was assassinated in 1963. While detractors say that means Congress must approve changes to the memorial, Trump has argued that he has the power to act.\"Simply put, Defendants cannot install memorials for President Trump or anyone or anything else at the Kennedy Center without Congress's blessing,\" US District Judge Christopher Cooper said in a written order issued on Tuesday.The judge said that the board's proposals to add language to the existing name of the centre and its surrounding campus \"bucks a federal court order and a statute Congress enacted\".That statute was a decision by the US legislative body to memorialise Kennedy, \"and no one else, at the Center bearing his name\", the order said.On Sunday, the Kennedy Center administration told its board that the arts institution was on the brink of bankruptcy, the Washington Post, external reported.The administration said it was in a \"precarious fiscal position\" and would not be able to support its payroll obligations and routine maintenance contracts \"within a matter of weeks\". The current leadership at the centre has said the building is unsafe for continued occupancy, pointing to part of the ceiling falling in earlier this month.  But others close to the centre dispute that it must be closed.The Kennedy Center did not immediately respond to the BBC's request for comment.Earlier on Tuesday, Trump confirmed the board would meet and said on Truth Social that the Kennedy Center is \"in a virtual state of collapse\".He described dire conditions in the building and railed against the \"hostile and conflicted\" judge for keeping it open despite neither having performances scheduled nor \"people that would have the Courage to even go in\".He also touted his ability to raise money and construction prowess, adding that he has the strength and power of the presidency to support his renovation.",
