      "id": "bbc-2026-09-14-watch-what-s-behind-the-decision-to-review-harry-and-meghan-",
      "title": "Watch: What's behind the decision to review Harry and Meghan's UK security?",
      "summary": "The Duke and Duchess of Sussex are going to be given a review of their publicly-funded security after their return to live in the UK.",
      "body": "The Duke and Duchess of Sussex are going to be given a review of their publicly-funded security after their return to live in the UK.The Sussexes have changed their children's school, only days after they first started, over security concerns about the school run.It is understood that the committee which oversees royal and VIP security, known as Ravec, is to reconsider Prince Harry and Meghan's level of police protection now that they and their two children are full-time residents rather than visitors.It will assess any risks they face in their new home and the type of trips taken by the couple and their family, such as regular travel routes and school runs.",
      "source": "BBC",
      "category": "world",
