      "id": "bbc-2026-09-14-americast",
      "title": "Americast",
      "summary": "And which songs have made it onto Trump’s Air Force One playlist?",
      "body": "Home            News            Sport            Weather            iPlayer            Sounds            Bitesize     CBeebies     CBBC     Food         Home     News     Sport     Business     Technology     Health     Culture     Arts     Travel     Earth     Audio     Video     Live          Use BBC.com or the new BBC App to listen to BBC podcasts, Radio 4 and the World Service outside the UK.Find out how to listen to other BBC stationsEpisode detailsNews,·14 Sep 2026,·31 minsAmericanswers… on 5 Live! Is Donald Trump the only regulation AI needs?AmericastAvailable for over a yearThe president is pushing back against calls from tech bosses to slow down the development of artificial intelligence. After claiming “whoever wins AI, wins” can Trump convince voters that greater regulation isn’t needed?\nAnd will Republican senator Mitch McConnell reappear as the senate reconvenes this week? The 84 year old has been absent after months of illness and, as conspiracy theories surrounding his wellbeing grow, he is facing mounting pressure to say whether he will return to his duties or resign.\nPlus, what’s on the president's hand-picked Air Force One playlist?\nJustin, Sarah and Sumi join Matt Chorley on 5 Live to answer your questions.\n• Justin Webb, Radio 4 presenter\n• Sarah Smith, North America Editor\n• Sumi Somaskanda, BBC Chief Presenter\n• Join our online community: https://discord.gg/qSrxqNcmRB\n• Send us a message or voice note via WhatsApp to +44 330 123 9480\nThis episode was made by Alix Pickles with Emma Close and Nik Sindle. The technical producer was Jonathan Greer. The series producer is Purvee Pattni. The senior news editor is Sam Bonham.\nIf you want to be notified every time we publish a new episode, please subscribe to us on BBC Sounds by hitting the subscribe button on the app.\nYou can now listen to Americast on a smart speaker. If you want to listen, just say \"Ask BBC Sounds to play Americast”. It works on most smart speakers.\nAmericast is part of the BBC News Podcasts family of podcasts. The team that makes Americast also makes lots of other podcasts, including Newscast. If you enjoy Americast (and if you're reading this then you hopefully do), then we think that you will enjoy some of our other pods too. See links below.\nThe Global Story: https://www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/brand/w13xtvsdProgramme WebsiteMore episodes",
