      "id": "theverge-2026-09-14-i-reviewed-valve-s-steam-frame-ask-me-anything",
      "title": "I reviewed Valve’s Steam Frame, ask me anything",
      "summary": "Hey! I'm Sean Hollister, you might have seen me around this place a few times, and I just spent three weeks beta-testing the Steam Frame, Valve's hotly anticipated new don't-call-it-a-VR-headset that might also be an early glimpse at the future of games that run everywhere. \nAt 4PM ET today (that's 1PM PT for West Coasters like me!), I will answer as many of your questions as humanly possible abou",
      "body": "Hey! I’m Sean Hollister, you might have seen me around this place a few times, and I just spent three weeks beta-testing the Steam Frame, Valve’s hotly anticipated new don’t-call-it-a-VR-headset that might also be an early glimpse at the future of games that run everywhere.\nAt 4PM ET today (that’s 1PM PT for West Coasters like me!), I will answer as many of your questions as humanly possible about this headset, its controllers, its ergonomic accessories kit, and the Arcturus Vision Camera. If you want me to test something special for you, get your question in ASAP — I’ll see if I can try it between now and then!\nWhile you wait, here are some of the answers we’ve collected so far:\n* Price, release date, reservation process, accessories\n* My video on what it’s like to be inside (also embedded at the bottom of this story soon)\n* Half-Life: Alyx reborn as a Steam Frame launch title\nI also figure some people might ask: “Did the Steam Frame really not leave a red ring on your face?” and I can answer that right now. I barely took it off during our lengthy photoshoot, and here’s what I looked like after:\n[Image: No red ring. https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/268694_Steam_Frame_KMcClellan_0048.jpg?quality=90&strip=all]\nSee you at 4PM ET!",
      "source": "The Verge",
      "category": "tech",
