      "id": "techcrunch-2026-09-13-larry-ellison-cancels-7-5-billion-sale-of-oracle-stock",
      "title": "Larry Ellison cancels $7.5 billion sale of Oracle stock",
      "summary": "Oracle had previously disclosed that Ellison planned to sell 50 million shares worth around $7.5 billion.",
      "body": "1:49 PM PDT · September 13, 2026\nImage Credits:Kim Kulish/Corbis / Getty Images\nOracle co-founder and executive chairman Larry Ellison has canceled a planned sale of his Oracle stock, the company announced on Saturday.\nOracle had previously disclosed in a regulatory filing that Ellison planned to sell 50 million shares worth around $7.5 billion, according to Reuters. The company did not offer a reason for the change in plans.\n“No Oracle stock was sold under that plan, and he has no other plans to sell any of his Oracle stock,” the company said.\nOracle stock is currently down 22% since the beginning of the year. The company has been spending heavily on data centers, and it recently became one of the major owners and security partners for TikTok’s U.S. operations.\nEllison has also used his wealth to back his son David’s acquisition of Warner Bros., which is currently being contested in court.\nSubscribe for the industry’s biggest tech news",
      "source": "TechCrunch",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [],
      "author": "Anthony Ha",
      "publishedAt": "2026-09-13T20:49:38.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://techcrunch.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/GettyImages-528022874.jpg?w=1024",
      "originalUrl": "https://techcrunch.com/2026/09/13/larry-ellison-cancels-7-5-billion-sale-of-oracle-stock/",
