      "id": "hackernews-2026-09-12-an-atlas-of-periodic-solutions-to-the-three-body-problem",
      "title": "An atlas of periodic solutions to the three-body problem",
      "summary": "Article URL: https://www.threebodyorbits.com/\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49670852\nPoints: 37\n# Comments: 0",
      "body": "An atlas of periodic solutions to the three-body problem.\nThe three-body problem has no general solution, but it has thousands of periodic orbits: three masses falling around each other and arriving, after one period, at precisely their starting positions and velocities.\nEvery one of the 3,915 orbits has a place on the map. Orbits that look alike sit next to each other; the families form islands, and each family has its own page. Far out the map is a constellation, close up each orbit runs live, and any orbit opens on its own page, where it plays one period at a time, can be nudged off its track, rated and ranked in battles.",
      "source": "Hacker News",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [],
      "author": "danielmorozoff",
      "publishedAt": "2026-09-12T10:13:24.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://www.threebodyorbits.com/images/atlas-og.png?v=20260908b",
      "originalUrl": "https://www.threebodyorbits.com/",
      "readTimeMinutes": 1,
      "language": "en"
