      "id": "bbc-2026-09-10-five-killed-and-67-injured-in-russian-strike-on-shopping-cen",
      "title": "Five killed and 67 injured in Russian strike on shopping centre, Ukraine says",
      "summary": "The attack in Pavlohrad city centre was the third Russian strike on a mall within days, local media report.",
      "body": "Images released by the State Emergency Service of Ukraine show firefighters directing water hoses at burning vehicles amid clouds of smoke on a street in Pavlohrad.In a Telegram post, regional governor Oleksandr Hanzha said of the 67 people injured, eight are children. Zelensky offered his condolences to the families and loved ones of those killed in Thursday's attack. \"The Russians used drones to kill people who were simply standing near shopping centres,\" Ukraine's president said in his statement.Ukrainian Foreign Minister Andrii Sybiha called the drone attack a \"tactic of coercion\". \"Russia believes that relentless attacks on civilians can exhaust Ukrainians and force Ukraine into concession,\" he said.Pavlohrad, a logistics hub near the central city of Dnipro, has come under heavy attack previously, with two people killed in an attack on warehouses there last month.  Ukrainian officials say a Russian drone attack on a mall in Sumy on Wednesday killed two people and wounded 20. On Thursday, Russian aerial bombing reportedly injured eight people in Sumy, including three children. In Zaporizhzhia, capital of the region of the same name which was partially annexed by Russia soon after the invasion, a shopping mall was almost completely destroyed on Monday, its owners reported.However, it was closed at the time and there were no immediate reports of casualties.  One of the bloodiest attacks on a shopping centre came last month, when Ukrainian officials say Russian drones killed at least 16 people and injured 130 in the city of Kryvyi Rih.",
      "source": "BBC",
      "category": "world",
      "tags": [],
      "author": null,
      "publishedAt": "2026-09-10T22:36:02.000Z",
