      "id": "techcrunch-2026-09-10-the-boring-company-raises-3b-in-round-led-by-uae",
      "title": "The Boring Company raises $3B in round led by UAE",
      "summary": "The company said it plans to dig more than 150 kilometers of tunnels in the Middle Eastern country.",
      "body": "8:07 AM PDT · September 10, 2026\nImage Credits:Ethan Miller / Getty Images\nElon Musk’s tunneling company, The Boring Company, has raised a $3 billion Series D funding round that pushes its valuation to $23 billion.\nThe round was led by the United Arab Emirates. The Boring Company said Thursday that it now plans to dig more than 150 kilometers of tunnels in the Middle Eastern country. Andreessen Horowitz, Sequoia Capital, Human Capital, Vy Capital, and Valor Equity Partners also participated.\nThe Wall Street Journal reported in July that The Boring Company was looking to raise as much as $4 billion.\nThe Boring Company has done most of its digging to date in Las Vegas, Nevada, where it operates a handful of tunnels that connect hotel casinos and the convention center. It recently started work on a project in Nashville, Tennessee, that will involve a 10-mile “loop” underground.\nThe company has stated that its goal is to “solve traffic” by moving vehicle travel into an underground, three-dimensional network of tunnels.\nSubscribe for the industry’s biggest tech news",
      "source": "TechCrunch",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [],
      "author": "Sean O'Kane",
      "publishedAt": "2026-09-10T15:07:27.000Z",
