      "body": "Homepage    Accessibility links   Skip to content   Accessibility Help     BBC Account      Notifications        Home            News            Sport            Weather            iPlayer            Sounds            Bitesize     CBeebies     CBBC     Food         Home     News     Sport     Business     Technology     Health     Culture     Arts     Travel     Earth     Audio     Video     Live               More menu             Search Sounds              Home            News            Sport            Weather            iPlayer            Sounds            Bitesize     CBeebies     CBBC     Food        Home     News     Sport     Business     Technology     Health     Culture     Arts     Travel     Earth     Audio     Video     Live         Close menu   BBC SoundsSounds home pageHomeMusicPodcastsMy SoundsUse BBC.com or the new BBC App to listen to BBC podcasts, Radio 4 and the World Service outside the UK.Find out how to listen to other BBC stationsEpisode detailsWorld Service,·08 Sep 2026,·26 minsThe copyright extortionistsTech LifeAvailable for over a yearLots of people make a living from social media posts. But some have been targeted by an international extortion scheme. It involves a flood of false copyright infringement claims. It only stops if the extorter is paid. Imran Rahman-Jones has the story.\nAlso this week: could AI help to spot wrong-way driving on Ireland's major roads? And we bring you the latest titles and tech on show at Gamescom in Germany.",
